<main><p class="eyebrow">NATHAN AI 🚀 · THE FORMULA OF LIFE APPLIED TO MINING</p>
<h1>Φ<sub>mine</sub> · Four-stage mining cycle</h1>
<p>Ca²⁺ activation → Zn²⁺ hashing → S_hard validation → C_init planning. This runs a genuine double-SHA-256 test against the <strong>historical Bitcoin genesis block</strong>, preserving all 21 authored coin rings. It does not create live mining shares or wallet rewards.</p>
<div class="stats">
<div class="stat"><small>Virtual address capacity</small><strong>732,000,000</strong><small>21 logical ring ranges, zero remote nodes</small></div>
<div class="stat"><small>Processing planes</small><strong>Alpha / Beta</strong><small>Candidate hashing and independent PoW verification</small></div>
<div class="stat"><small>Original cost target</small><strong>16:1</strong><small>Design benchmark, not realized mining profit</small></div>
</div>
<section class="panel"><h2>1. Launch an authorized local header test</h2>
<form id="job-form"><div class="form-grid">
<label for="start-nonce">Nonce start<input id="start-nonce" type="number" min="0" max="4294967295" value="2083236891" step="1"></label>
<label for="attempts">Candidates (1–256)<input id="attempts" type="number" min="1" max="256" value="5" step="1"></label>
</div>
<label><input id="consent" type="checkbox" style="width:auto;margin-right:9px">I authorize this local, bounded proof-of-work test; no wallet, pool, miner, or node is contacted.</label>
<div><button id="run-cycle" type="submit">Run all four stages</button><button id="one-step" type="button" class="secondary">Run next stage</button><button id="reset-cycle" type="button" class="secondary">Reset</button><button id="export-cycle" type="button" class="secondary" disabled>Export audit JSON</button></div>
</form><p role="status" id="status">Ready. Authorize the test to begin.</p>
<div class="stages" id="stage-grid"></div></section>
<section class="panel"><h2>2. Alpha / Beta cryptographic results</h2>
<pre id="results">No blocks hashed yet.</pre><p class="note">The historical nonce 2083236893 verifies a publicly known valid Bitcoin genesis header. Finding this nonce in a historical test vector is not earning BTC or mining a new network block.</p></section>
<section class="panel"><h2>3. Whole-number workload map</h2><p>There is no 732-million-process launch. Each range is an arithmetic address interval associated with the existing authored coin identifier, not an external currency or mining network.</p>
<div style="overflow:auto"><table><thead><tr><th>Ring</th><th>Name</th><th>Logical positions</th><th>Network</th></tr></thead><tbody id="rings"></tbody></table></div></section>
<section class="panel"><h2>4. Measured electricity comparison</h2><p>Use the same observation window for pool-confirmed output, meter-measured kWh and your actual electric rate. No data is invented.</p>
<div class="form-grid"><label>Verified output USD<input id="usd-output" type="number" min="0" step="any" placeholder="Example: 16"></label>
<label>Measured kWh<input id="kwh" type="number" min="0" step="any" placeholder="Example: 2"></label>
<label>Rate USD/kWh<input id="rate" type="number" min="0" step="any" placeholder="Example: 0.5"></label></div>
<button id="efficiency" type="button">Calculate measured ratio</button><p id="efficiency-result">Measured inputs required.</p>
<p><a href="../integrations/index.html">Open read-only mining, pool, wallet, and power monitoring connections</a></p></section>
<p class="note"><strong>Original-source boundary:</strong> Ca²⁺/Zn²⁺ here are lifecycle metaphors. The code uses SHA-256d and a bounded schedule. It does not awaken AI, bypass Bitcoin difficulty, deploy proxies, change power states, move coins, lock out a root operator or modify itself.</p></main>
<footer><small>NATHAN AI → TABOR ROOT → TABOR 1-2-3 FACTORY → ONE · Additive implementation; no existing modules replaced.</small></footer></body></html>